Virtual prototypes are high fidelity digital models that replicate the geometry, material behavior, and functional performance of physical products throughout the design cycle. These simulations enable engineers to assess fit and function, structural integrity, and manufacturing feasibility before any hardware is built. The technology offers early defect detection, improved compliance, and streamlined collaboration across disciplines, thereby reducing time to market and product development costs.
What is a Virtual Prototype?
A Virtual Prototype refers to a computer generated, digital representation of a product that captures physical attributes, operational dynamics, and environmental interactions. By enabling engineers to simulate impacts, thermal flows, fatigue, and fluid dynamics, virtual prototypes provide an integrated platform for testing design hypotheses, optimizing components, and validating performance against stringent regulatory criteria. This digital simulation mirrors or even surpasses the capabilities of traditional physical mocks, allowing for rapid iteration and cross functional validation within the same virtual environment.
